.\" Manual page for explore(1). Written to exercise every field the roff
.\" plugin extracts: a full title macro, several sections, a synopsis, an
.\" options list, an example and cross-references.
.TH EXPLORE 1 "September 2026" "Repos Explorer 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
explore \- a front door to the working directories source control checks out
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B explore
[\fB\-\-root\fR \fIDIRECTORY\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-status\fR]
[\fIPATH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B explore
opens at the configured Repos Directory and lists the repositories inside
it, reading each one's provider, branch and working-tree state from the
checkout's own files.
.PP
It never runs a source control command. Clone, fetch, pull and commit are
deliberately out of scope.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-root " " \fIDIRECTORY\fR
Open at \fIDIRECTORY\fR instead of the configured Repos Directory. An
explicit instruction, not a remembered location.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-status
Skip the working-tree comparison, which reads the index of the selected
repository.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The window closed normally.
.TP
.B 2
The Repos Directory could not be read.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/RepoSphereExplorer/repos.json
The configured roots, with exactly one marked active.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR ls (1),
.BR find (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by the dark factory.
